        <mxCell id="r35" value="- path: std::string" style="text;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;overflow=hidden;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;rotatable=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Courier New;" vertex="1" parent="c34"><mxGeometry y="30" width="540" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s36" value="" style="line;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingTop=-1;spacingLeft=3;spacingRight=3;rotatable=0;labelPosition=right;points=[];portConstraint=eastwest;strokeColor=inherit;" vertex="1" parent="c34"><mxGeometry y="56" width="540" height="8" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="r37" value="+ getPath(): std::string" style="text;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;overflow=hidden;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;rotatable=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Courier New;" vertex="1" parent="c34"><mxGeometry y="64" width="540" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="b38" value="&lt;b&gt;No FTP_Directory exists.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The FTP side passes plain std::string paths around, so the caller has to build every path itself." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;darkOpacity=0.05;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;fontSize=12;size=14;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="648" width="540" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="b39" value="&lt;b&gt;The problem:&lt;/b&gt; there is no line between the left and the right half - the two classes share no common type.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• The same five steps are implemented twice (runFtpDemo / runSftpDemo).&lt;br&gt;• No function can take “a connection”, because no such type exists. The two objects cannot even be put into one std::vector, so main() has to call both demo functions by name. A template does not help either: the method &lt;i&gt;names&lt;/i&gt; already differ.&lt;br&gt;• The error conventions disagree - &lt;i&gt;if (ftp.open())&lt;/i&gt; is correct, &lt;i&gt;if (sftp.connect())&lt;/i&gt; is a bug, and both compile.&lt;br&gt;• A third protocol (FTPS) means a third copy of everything." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;darkOpacity=0.05;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;fontSize=12;size=14;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="838" width="1160" height="175" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e40" value="uses" style="endArrow=open;endFill=0;endSize=12;dashed=1;html=1;rounded=0;strokeColor=#7f7f7f;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="b2" target="c4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e41" value="uses" style="endArrow=open;endFill=0;endSize=12;dashed=1;html=1;rounded=0;strokeColor=#7f7f7f;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="b3" target="c19"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e42" value="returns / takes" style="endArrow=open;endFill=0;endSize=12;dashed=1;html=1;rounded=0;strokeColor=#7f7f7f;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c19" target="c34"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
